13
00:01:59,470 --> 00:02:02,500
Rectangle perimeter:

14
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:25,330
To calculate rectangle perimeter we take length plus width (same unit) then multiply by 2.

15
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:42,460
Example: Calculate perimeter of rectangle with length 12 cm, width 5 cm.

16
00:02:47,290 --> 00:03:02,290
Apply rectangle perimeter rule we take (12 + 5) x 2

17
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:09,760
Rectangle perimeter is 34 cm.

18
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,330
Square perimeter:

19
00:03:19,450 --> 00:03:29,600
To calculate square perimeter we take side length times 4.

20
00:03:34,570 --> 00:03:46,570
Example: Calculate perimeter of a square brick with side 20 cm.

21
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:57,050
Apply square perimeter rule.

22
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:11,450
Square brick perimeter is: 20 x 4 = 80 (cm)

